(THE HINDU MARRIAGE ACT, 1955) '
(Act No. 25 of 1955 Enacted on 18th May, 1955) '
(Official Gazette of India - Ministry of Law and Justice Legislative Department) '
(Repository: India Code indiacode.nic.in) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(Section 2: Application of Act - Applies to Hindus, Buddhists, Jains, and Sikhs.) '
(Section 5: Conditions for a Hindu Marriage Monogamy, Sound Mind, Age 21/18.) '
(Section 7: Ceremonies for a Hindu Marriage Saptapadi and Customary Rites.) '
(Section 8: Registration of Hindu Marriages.) '
(Section 9: Restitution of Conjugal Rights.) '
(Section 10: Judicial Separation.) '
(Section 11: Void Marriages Null and Void Ab Initio - Bigamy, Prohibited Degrees.) '
(Section 12: Voidable Marriages Impotency, Unsound Mind, Force/Fraud, Pregnancy.) '
(Section 13: Divorce Adultery, Cruelty, Desertion 2+ Years, Unsound Mind, Conversion.) '
(Section 13B: Divorce by Mutual Consent 1 Year Separation, 6-18 Months Motion.) '
(Section 14: No Petition for Divorce within One Year of Marriage.) '
(Section 16: Legitimacy of Children of Void and Voidable Marriages.) '
(Section 17: Punishment of Bigamy.) '
(Section 24: Maintenance Pendente Lite and Expenses of Proceedings Interim Relief.) '
(Section 25: Permanent Alimony and Maintenance.) '
(Section 26: Custody of Children.) '
(Section 27: Disposal of Property Joint Property and Stridhan Safeguards.) '
(Section 28: Appeals from Decrees and Orders 90-day limitation period.) '
